WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.290
The European Union has launched its mission
to help Ukraine reform its civilian security

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:12.629
sector - police, border authorities, intelligence
services and justice system.

00:00:12.629 --> 00:00:17.590
From the capital Kyiv, dozens of senior officials
and officers from around Europe are working

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:21.900
to build trust with their counterparts in
Ukraine’s interior ministry, the security

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.410
sector, and courts.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:30.060
This is not a training mission, nor is anyone
armed. It’s about providing strategic advice

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.590
to Ukrainian officials on anything to do with
the rule of law, except for defence matters.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:43.800
By March, more than 100 international and about 75 local staff
are due to be working from the EU Advisory

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.830
Mission’s new headquarters, counselling
and mentoring officials in Ukraine’s civilian

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.110
security sector.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:56.110
For the moment, the search for the right building
goes on, just one of EUAM’s many challenges.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.760
In the few months since a fact-finding team
arrived, staff have been talking with their

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:06.620
local counterparts and civic partners - listening,
forging relationships, trying to understand

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.770
how best to help Ukraine, even as conflict
simmers in the east.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.790
SOUNDBITE - Kalman Mizsei, EUAM Ukraine Head of Mission

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:21.420
“It's not an easy job. It's going to take
a lot of time. How far we go in two years,

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:29.370
nobody at this moment can tell."

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.240
Trust must be re-established between the police
forces and the people. Public confidence was

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.380
never particularly high, but the heavy police
handling of the pro-European Maidan rallies

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.479
a year ago made things worse.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:47.549
Corruption is the biggest challenge the EU
mission faces. Low wages, a lack of checks

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:52.250
and balances, and a vertical structure that
leaves the policeman on the street unaware

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.760
of interior ministry priorities provide room
for corruption to flourish.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.290
Ukraine is setting up an anti-corruption bureau
to help restore confidence.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:07.869
For it to work, EU officials say, policies
must be clear and transparent, with easy public

00:02:07.869 --> 00:02:12.590
access to reliable information. It’s a problem
that cannot be fixed overnight.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.279
SOUNDBITE - Mika Aalto, EUAM Ukraine Anti-corruption
Advisor

00:02:14.279 --> 00:02:20.269
“Ukrainian society is vulnerable for corruption,
there is no doubt about that. We all are aware

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:27.269
about the fact. But I think that the biggest
problem is that normal people, they don't

00:02:27.859 --> 00:02:38.379
trust the decisions-makers. And we need to
find ways in order to convince the decision-makers

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:44.139
to make such decisions so that Ukrainian people
can find the trust in the Ukrainian authorities

00:02:44.139 --> 00:02:45.029
again."

00:02:45.029 --> 00:02:49.299
While the effects of the conflict are not
obvious in Kyiv, the fighting does bring social

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:54.709
tensions, and internally displaced people.
Still, the government remains willing to reform

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:57.010
the security sector.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.450
Reform of agencies like the traffic police
is being carried out under the Association

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.889
Agreement that is the foundation stone of
Ukraine’s relations with the European Union.

00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:12.620
That means getting EUAM staff as close as
possible to all the security wings, including

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:16.680
the intelligence service, the riot police,
or the border guards.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:23.419
Ukraine has 7,000 kilometres of borders,
about a third of that shared with Russia.

00:03:23.419 --> 00:03:28.829
The border police were the first hit by the
conflict. They seem optimistic about cooperating

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:29.829
with the European mission.

00:03:29.829 --> 00:03:31.620
SOUNDBITE - Colonel Yulia Petrova, Ukraine
State Border Guard Service

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:37.559
"The Ukrainian border guards are very committed
to move on reforms toward European standards.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:46.040
And we really hope this EU mission will be
of great help to do that, and to achieve this

00:03:46.109 --> 00:03:47.230
goal."

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:53.559
But this is just the start. EUAM is a long-term
project. The mission has a two-year mandate

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:59.669
and a first-year budget of just over 13 million
euros. Staff will conduct a strategic assessment

00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:00.859
in 12 months.

00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:06.969
For now, the focus is on building relationships
and establishing trust, between the EU mission

00:04:06.969 --> 00:04:12.359
and the Ukrainian security sector, but also
on restoring citizens’ confidence in their

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:13.639
forces of order.

00:04:13.639 --> 00:04:19.669
Because people expect change. They want assurances
that Ukraine’s security forces have turned

00:04:19.669 --> 00:04:22.339
their backs on the old ways of the past.

